{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>One pan of ten gold.</b> Corresponding to the Ten Commandments that Moses received, which are filled with fine fragrance like the incense offering. And one can prove from here what the Sages said, that the cup of birkat ha-mazon is worth forty gold coins — this is the meaning of the verse: 'one' from כ\"ף, that is, the one hundred blessings a person is obligated to recite every day, as the numerical value of כ\"ף. 'Ten gold' is worth ten gold coins, and if so, the cup of blessing, which contains four blessings, is worth forty gold coins."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:48.809048299Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}